  "problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\n- $1$\n- $-\\sqrt{18}$\n- $\\sqrt{6}$\n- $0$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that ${Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $1$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{18}=-3\\sqrt{2}$ is a not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\sqrt{6}$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $0$ is not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\".",
